Quick care reminders for Genovese basil:
- Light: 6–8 hours direct sun (south-facing window) or 12–14 hours under a grow light.
- Pot/soil: 6–8" pot with good drainage; use a well-draining potting mix.
- Water: keep soil evenly moist but not waterlogged — water when top 1" feels dry.
- Temperature: 65–85°F (18–29°C); avoid cold drafts.
- Feeding: balanced liquid fertilizer every 4–6 weeks at half strength.
